What is Prometheus?

Prometheus is an open-source monitoring and alerting system designed for modern cloud and container environments.
It collects metrics from your servers, applications, and Kubernetes clusters in real time.
Think of Prometheus as the heart of your monitoring stack 

📊 What are Metrics?
Metrics are numbers that tell you how your system behaves.
Examples:
• CPU usage
• Memory consumption
• Disk usage
• HTTP request count
• Error rate
• API response time

Prometheus continuously collects these numbers every few seconds.

⚙️ How Prometheus Works (Simple Flow)
1️⃣ Prometheus scrapes metrics from targets
(servers, apps, containers)
2️⃣ Stores them as time-series data
3️⃣ Lets you query the data using PromQL
4️⃣ Sends alerts when something goes wrong 🚨

🔍 What makes Prometheus powerful?
✨ Pull-based monitoring (scraping)
✨ Powerful query language → PromQL
✨ Built-in alerting system
✨ Perfect for Kubernetes & microservices
✨ Service discovery (auto detect targets)

This is why Prometheus became the standard monitoring tool in cloud-native world.

🚨 Real DevOps Example
Your application suddenly becomes slow.
Prometheus can show:
• Request latency increased
• Error rate spiked
• Pod CPU usage at 95%
• Memory nearing limit
Instead of guessing → you get data-driven troubleshooting.

🤝 Prometheus + Grafana = Perfect Combo
Prometheus → Collects & stores metrics
Grafana → Visualizes those metrics
Together they create a complete observability stack 🔥

💡 Final Thought
Without monitoring, failures become surprises.
With Prometheus, failures become alerts.
